  "title": "COP31 Climate Talks in Turkiye: Deadlock Over Fossil Fuels",
  "summary": "Countries from nearly 200 countries are in a deadlock to try and get a new global climate agreement, with work crews at the venue of the annual climate talks in Turkiye boxing up the venue as negotiators go into overtime. The talks, scheduled to end Friday, face strong condemnation for failing to include fossil fuels in the draft document.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "COP31 climate talks in Turkiye, as described in the report, involve countries in a deadlock to finalize a new global climate agreement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Work crews were boxing up the venue of the talks, highlighting the effort to reach a final agreement despite ongoing negotiations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The talks faced strong condemnation from activists and some countries for not including fossil fuels in the final document.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
